.TH "provision-samba-ad-dc" "8" "2026-09-11" "ltsp6"
.SH "NAME"
provision\-samba\-ad\-dc \(em Provision the Samba AD domain controller the lab authenticates against
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBprovision\-samba\-ad\-dc\fR \fIip/cidr\fR \fIgateway\fR \fIrealm\fR \fInetbios\fR \fIadminpass\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Run on the machine that is to become the domain controller, as root. It pins
the static address, fixes /etc/hosts, provisions the domain with
\fB\-\-use\-rfc2307\fR, sets a DNS forwarder, points the host's own resolver at
itself and verifies the result.
.PP
Everything else in the lab authenticates against this host, so it is built
first. Nothing after it will work until \fBhost \-t SRV
_ldap._tcp.\fR\fIdomain\fR returns an answer.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
.IP "\fIip/cidr\fP" 4
The static address, for example 172.17.250.10/20.
.IP "\fIgateway\fP" 4
Default gateway.
.IP "\fIrealm\fP" 4
Kerberos realm in upper case, for example LTSPLAB.LOCAL.
.IP "\fInetbios\fP" 4
NetBIOS domain name, for example LTSPLAB.
.IP "\fIadminpass\fP" 4
Password for the domain Administrator account. Subject to the default
complexity policy \(em at least seven characters with mixed classes.
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.PP
.nf
provision\-samba\-ad\-dc 172.17.250.10/20 172.17.240.1 \
    LTSPLAB.LOCAL LTSPLAB '<admin\-password>'
.fi
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
The script refuses to continue if the host holds more than one address. That
is not fussiness: a domain controller that answers DNS from an address the
client did not ask has every reply discarded, and the symptom is not a DNS
error but domain members that intermittently cannot find the realm. Debian 13
ships \fBdhcpcd\fR, started by ifupdown rather than as a systemd unit, so
\fBsystemctl is\-enabled dhcpcd\fR reports \fInot\-found\fR while several
dhcpcd processes are running and holding a second address.
.PP
It \fIsets\fR the DNS forwarder rather than checking whether the line exists.
An earlier version tested for the presence of \fBdns forwarder\fR in smb.conf
and left the value at \fBnone\fR, which looks configured and forwards nothing.
.SH "VERIFICATION"
.PP
.nf
samba\-tool domain level show
host \-t SRV _ldap._tcp.ltsplab.local
host \-t SRV _kerberos._udp.ltsplab.local
kinit administrator && klist
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBsetup\-ltsp\-app\fP(8),
\fBsetup\-home\-server\fP(8),
\fBsamba\-tool\fP(8),
\fBadcli\fP(8),
/usr/share/doc/ltsp\-server/HOWTO\-lab\-from\-scratch.
.SH "AVAILABILITY"
.PP
